in","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Unelli_quater_stater_Gallica_celtiques_884_revers.jpg"}},"uyghur-khaganate":{"img":"/images/states/uyghur-khaganate.jpg","cr":{"a":"8th century Manichean painter","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Conversion_of_B%C3%B6g%C3%BC_Qaghan_(759-780_CE)_to_Manicheism_in_762_(detailed_of_B%C3%B6g%C3%BC_Qaghan_in_a_suit_of_armour,_kneeling_to_a_Manichean_high_priest).jpg"}},"uqaylid-dynasty":{"img":"/images/states/uqaylid-dynasty.jpg","cr":{"a":"Ali Zifan","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uqaylid_dynasty_(greatest_extent).svg"}},"upper-aulaqi-sultanate":{"img":"/images/states/upper-aulaqi-sultanate.jpg","cr":{"a":"","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FederationOfSouthArabiaMap.jpg"}},"ukrainian-peoples-republic-of-soviets":{"img":"/images/states/ukrainian-peoples-republic-of-soviets.jpg","cr":{"a":"I Gauravjuvekar vectorized the above file.","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ukrainian_People%27s_Republic_of_the_Soviets.svg"}},"usdiae":{"t":"People of south-eastern Ireland known only from Ptolemy\u0027s Geography, placed inland near the Brigantes and Coriondi.","o":"The Usdiae appear in Ptolemy\u0027s Geography of about 150 in the south-east of Ireland, inland of the coastal Brigantes (Ireland) and Manapii and near the Coriondi, roughly in the region of modern Kilkenny, Carlow or Laois. As with all of Ptolemy\u0027s Irish names, the data came second-hand from earlier sea reports.","r":"Nothing is recorded of their rulers, settlements or way of life, and no convincing link has been found between their name and any people of early Irish tradition. The fertile lands of the Barrow and Nore valleys in this region supported mixed farming and cattle-raising.","e":"The Usdiae do not appear again in any source. The region where Ptolemy placed them later belonged to the Kingdom of Osraige and the Kingdom of Leinster.","re":"Celtic polytheism","la":"Goidelic Celtic","c":"low"},"united-kingdom":{"img":"/images/states/united-kingdom.jpg","cr":{"a":"Original: Acts of Union 1800 Vector: Zscout370","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_United_Kingdom_(1-2).svg"}},"uyunid-emirate":{"img":"/images/states/uyunid-emirate.jpg","cr":{"a":"Aziz911q8","l":"CC0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uyunids.jpg"}},"united-belgian-states":{"img":"/images/states/united-belgian-states.jpg","cr":{"a":"TRAJAN 117 This W3C-unspecified vector image was created with Inkscape .","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:United_States_of_Belgium_(1790).svg"}},"uesugi-clan-domain":{"img":"/images/states/uesugi-clan-domain.jpg","cr":{"a":"Mukai","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Japanese_Crest_Uesugi_Sasa.svg"}},"upper-yafa-sultanate":{"img":"/images/states/upper-yafa-sultanate.jpg","cr":{"a":"Xwejnusgozo","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_State_of_Upper_Yafa.svg"}},"united-states-army-military-government-in-korea":{"img":"/images/states/united-states-army-military-government-in-korea.jpg","cr":{"a":"Created by jacobolus using Adobe Illustrator.","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_United_States_(1912-1959).svg"}},"umbrians":{"t":"Italic people of central Italy, called by Pliny the oldest in Italy, whose ritual Iguvine Tablets are the longest surviving text in any Italic language other than Latin.","o":"The Umbrians lived in the upper Tiber valley and the Apennines east of Etruria from the early 1st millennium BCE. Ancient writers believed they had once held a much larger area before being pushed back by Etruscans and Gauls. They spoke Umbrian, an Osco-Umbrian language.","r":"Umbrian communities were independent towns and hill sanctuaries, among them Iguvium, Tuder, Asisium, Mevania, Spoletium and Ameria, without a lasting central government. The Iguvine Tablets, seven bronze plates of the 3rd to 1st centuries BCE, set out the rituals of the Atiedian Brethren, a priestly college of Iguvium, giving rich detail on Italic religion. Bronze votive figures from mountain shrines are typical of their art.","e":"Rome founded Narnia in 299 BCE, and after the battle of Sentinum in 295 BCE, where some Umbrians backed the anti-Roman coalition, the Umbrian towns became allies. The last resistance, at Sarsina, ended in 266 BCE. They gained citizenship after the Social War, and the name survives in the Italian region of Umbria.","re":"Umbrian polytheism","la":"Umbrian","c":"medium","img":"/images/states/umbrians.jpg","cr":{"a":"Italy_400bC_It.svg: Decan derivative work: Richardprins (talk)","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Italy_400bC_en.svg"}},"unitarian-league":{"img":"/images/states/unitarian-league.jpg","cr":{"a":"KaasterMDK","l":"CC BY 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Argentina_en_Enero_de_1831,_durante_la_Tercera_Guerra_Civil_Argentina.png"}},"united-arab-emirates":{"img":"/images/states/united-arab-emirates.jpg","cr":{"a":"Abdulla Mohammed Al Maainah","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_United_Arab_Emirates.svg"}},"ukrainian-ssr":{"img":"/images/states/ukrainian-ssr.jpg","cr":{"a":"Zscout370 and others. All authors are listed in the \"File versions\" section below.","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Ukrainian_Soviet_Socialist_Republic_(1949%E2%80%931991).svg"}},"united-states-military-government-of-the-philippine-islands":{"img":"/images/states/united-states-military-government-of-the-philippine-islands.jpg","cr":{"a":"No machine-readable author provided. Jacobolus assumed (based on copyright claims).","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_United_States_(1896%E2%80%931908).svg"}},"upper-canada":{"img":"/images/states/upper